{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/481333-need-help-coming-up-with-the-ban-bane-of-an-angel","id":481333,"title":"Need help coming up with the Ban & Bane of an angel","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-15T09:01:39-07:00","id":481333,"title":"Need help coming up with the Ban & Bane of an angel","content":"I'm running a Vampire/Demon crossover game set in Berlin (specifically the Margraviate of Berlin-Brandenburg as detailed in <i>Vampire The Requiem 2nd Edition</i>). The mysterious vampire killer that's been plaguing the city's Kindred for over a decade is actually an angel, known to the Kindred as Abaddon (real name: Antibody, goes by Jonathan Morris or Charlotte Aulin depending on its Manifestation).<br /> <br /> Its creation was in part thanks to a ritual performed by a cult of Holy Engineers in the Lancea et Sanctum, presumably after receiving visions or omens or messages from a psychopomp angel, or just plain crazy vampireness. I'm giving Antibody a lot of Strix-y mystique. True form is smoky, its shadow while Manifest probably has owl &quot;horns&quot;, big yellow eyes. It harvests all of the Vitae and the Soul of a target vampire by slicing open their heart and inhaling the soul as it tries to escape, in a rather Diablerie-esque ritual.<br /> <br /> Then it takes the harvested goods back to its Facility to convert into weapons and upgrades for itself, which it uses to track down Unchained.<br /> <br /> Here's what I've got for it so far:<br /> <br /> <b>Antibody<br /> Vampire-killing Angel of Redemption</b><br /> a.k.a. Abaddon, Jonathan Morris, Charlotte Aulin<br /> <b>Rank</b> 4<br /> <b>Virtue</b> Forgiveness<br /> <b>Vice</b> Single-Minded<br /> <b>Attributes: </b>Power 10, Finesse 12, Resistance 9<br /> <b>Influences: </b>Blood 3, Darkness 2<br /> <b>Corpus </b>14<br /> <b>Willpower </b>10<br /> <b>Initiative</b> 21<br /> <b>Defense</b> 10<br /> <b>Armor </b>0<br /> <b>Speed </b>27 (I'm not quite sure if I calculated this right: Power + Finesse + Size?)<br /> <b>Numina: </b>Strike Blind, Drain, Host Jump, Speed, Innocuous, Awe, Seek, Kindred Disciplines (as Strix Dread Power: VtR2E page 211) (Auspex 2, Obfuscate 2)<br /> <b>Manifestations: </b>Twilight Form, Materialize, Possess, Possess Corpse (as Strix Embodiment: VtR2E page 204), Discorporate<br /> <b>Max Essence</b> 25<br /> <br /> I figure its ban and bane should be something related to its connection with vampires. Perhaps it suffers damage from the sun like a Kindred or a Strix? Can't Manifest (or alternately, stay in Twilight) during the day? Perhaps the bane should be something related to fire, but appropriate for its rank. Literally a flaming holy sword, or perhaps it takes Aggravated damage from one of its &quot;fathers&quot; (as a symbolic reference to the Binding of Isaac; the &quot;fathers&quot; in this case would refer to the Holy Engineers who helped create it)?<br /> <br /> Powerful ephemeral entities are hard for me to come up with good bans and banes for, and Angels most of all. So some ideas would be appreciated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-15T10:44:34-07:00","id":481401,"title":"","content":"<b>Bane</b>: Fangs (and claws) of a vampire. In fact, you could make a sword out of vampire teeth and it would be a gruesome weapon against this angel.<br /> <b>Ban</b>: Must follow trails of blood to the end.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3855-gebbethine","name":"gebbethine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-15T11:09:01-07:00","id":481413,"title":"","content":"You're certainly on the right track with the Bans and Banes. That said using vampire-like Bans/Banes makes it more like the Strix is appears similar to, losing the element of trickery inherent in this angel. That said, it's always fun for sunlight and fire to be a vampire's best weapon against a foe.. I'd advise treating the rules on rarity of bans/Banes based on Rank as guidelines - most example angels certainly do. <br /> <br /> Other options -<br /> It can't harm anybody that surrenders (fits with Forgiveness and its more martial aspects), it's repulsed by the cries of owls, human blood is a bane to it, it requires permission to enter any privately-owned building, it cannot Discorporate after feeding (until it reaches its Infrastructure, anyways)...<br /> Maybe play up the origins of this angel as a clue. Give it Christian-themed weaknesses - it's banished by crosses, vulnerable to wine or must spare those who quote scripture. Perhaps any spear is a bane to it. <br /> <br /> I think you've got the Vice and Virtue mixed up, BTW. Angelic Vice and Virtue are from the God-Machine's perspective if I remember correctly, making Forgiveness a clear Vice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Onyx Path Freelancer: Demon Storyteller's Guide, Dark Eras, Night Horrors: Enemy Action</i><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Guide Extra Material</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/899423-after-the-fall-bonus-material\" target=\"_blank\">After the Fall: Bonus Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","name":"Eremite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-15T17:57:11-07:00","id":481790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eremite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/481333-need-help-coming-up-with-the-ban-bane-of-an-angel?p=481413#post481413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you've got the Vice and Virtue mixed up, BTW. Angelic Vice and Virtue are from the God-Machine's perspective if I remember correctly, making Forgiveness a clear Vice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Angelic Virtue and Vice can run the gamut of both lists of examples from the GMC update as well as things that have no clear correlation to good or evil, like &quot;Pristine.&quot; Both versions of Y2K have &quot;Contrary&quot; as a Virtue or a Vice, for example. I think it's one of the neater ways to replicate effects like &quot;ghosts/Fae/the Lilithim flip their rates of Willpower recovery from Virtue and Vice.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T08:27:20-07:00","id":482396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eremite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/481333-need-help-coming-up-with-the-ban-bane-of-an-angel?p=481413#post481413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Other options -<br /> It can't harm anybody that surrenders (fits with Forgiveness and its more martial aspects), it's repulsed by the cries of owls, human blood is a bane to it, it requires permission to enter any privately-owned building, it cannot Discorporate after feeding (until it reaches its Infrastructure, anyways)...<br /> Maybe play up the origins of this angel as a clue. Give it Christian-themed weaknesses - it's banished by crosses, vulnerable to wine or must spare those who quote scripture. Perhaps any spear is a bane to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm feeling something on spears as a bane, though I feel like &quot;any spear&quot; is too common for a Rank 4. The book describes the banes for rank 4 and 5 ephemeral entities as &quot;[H]ighly-specific banes that require great effort to acquire[...] A high Rank angel can't willingly touch the sigils of a certain incantation in Sumerian and dies if the signs are carved into the flesh of its host.&quot;<br /> <br /> So perhaps The Spear of Longinus would make a good bane. The problem there is that now I have to create that, and we're getting close to making Judeo-Christian stuff canon (in my setting that's simply a no-no). Perhaps a spear fashioned out of the bones of a &quot;penitent Damned&quot;. Which reminds me that one of the players is a Status (Lancea et Sanctum) 3 Kindred with Penitent as his Dirge. I'm liking this.<br /> <br /> Ban-wise, the example they give is &quot;The angel Uriminel, four-faced enforcer of destiny, has Defense 0 against individuals who have suffered lethal or aggravated damage within the last lunar month.&quot;<br /> <br /> I actually really like the &quot;cannot Discorporate after feeding&quot; less as a Ban and more as a matter of practicality: It can't Discorporate because it's containing a vampire's soul and Vitae. Discorporating would cause that to be destroyed or freed or whatever, which would be bad. I'll think on it. Perhaps its ban is that it suffers a Defense penalty equal to an attacking vampire's Status (Lancea et Sanctum) rank? Hmm. Alternatively, being repulsed by mortal blood (blood from a Demon's cover wouldn't count), repulsed by the touch of a &quot;pure&quot; human (Integrity 8+; as the vampire bane), or must accept a surrender from those who beg for forgiveness are also really good, I think.<br /> <br /> Thanks for the advice and ideas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T09:07:25-07:00","id":482442,"title":"","content":"Again, I'd really take the high-Rank Banes thing with a pinch of salt. The Lambent from Demon: The Descent's weakness is a piece of linchpin-phone from his bridge - specific, but not insanely so. From GMC we have Mr Nose, Rank 4, with latex as a bane. Black Nathaniel, Rank 5, has white marble as his.<br /> <br /> That said, a spear made from the bones of Kindred is a pretty awesome Bane, tricky to come by without being impossible. If you're unscrupulous you can find or make a suitable vampire and harvest their bones... You can even use your own bones, if you fit the profile. I like it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Onyx Path Freelancer: Demon Storyteller's Guide, Dark Eras, Night Horrors: Enemy Action</i><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Guide Extra Material</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/899423-after-the-fall-bonus-material\" target=\"_blank\">After the Fall: Bonus Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","name":"Eremite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T09:18:57-07:00","id":482449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eremite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/481333-need-help-coming-up-with-the-ban-bane-of-an-angel?p=482442#post482442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, I'd really take the high-Rank Banes thing with a pinch of salt. The Lambent from Demon: The Descent's weakness is a piece of linchpin-phone from his bridge - specific, but not insanely so. From GMC we have Mr Nose, Rank 4, with latex as a bane. Black Nathaniel, Rank 5, has white marble as his.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seeing as I have all of those books, I really should do a better job of looking at the examples.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That said, a spear made from the bones of Kindred is a pretty awesome Bane, tricky to come by without being impossible. If you're unscrupulous you can find or make a suitable vampire and harvest their bones... You can even use your own bones, if you fit the profile. I like it. </div> </div> </div>Exactly. I think it'll be interesting. Especially since the Demons in the party already think that they've turned one of the vampires in the party into &quot;bait&quot; by sending him into a store that they confirmed was Infrastructure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}